hls: a playlist load that fails half way drops its kept-alive connection

With http_persistent (the default) a playlist reload reuses the
connection the last load read its answer on. A load that failed before
the end of the answer (a garbled line, which 0102 plays through on a
live reload) left the rest of that answer unread on the connection, and
the next reload read it first: no "#EXTM3U" line, so that reload failed
too, and so on, a line of the old answer at a time (in the fixture, three
garbled answers made 13 failed reloads).

Close the kept-alive connection when a load fails; the next load opens a
new one.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -1510,6 +1510,10 @@ fail:
     av_free(new_url);
     if (close_in)
         ff_format_io_close(c->ctx, &in);
+    else if (ret < 0 && in && in == *playlist_pb)
+        /* a load that failed half way left the rest of the answer on the
+         * kept-alive connection, which the next load would read first */
+        ff_format_io_close(c->ctx, playlist_pb);
     c->ctx->ctx_flags = c->ctx->ctx_flags & ~(unsigned)AVFMTCTX_UNSEEKABLE;
     if (!c->n_variants || !c->variants[0]->n_playlists ||
         !c->variants[0]->playlists[0]->n_segments)
